IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P2-section-2-gate`

-- P2-art-12: Article 12 (record-keeping) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744. The Omnibus did not change Article 12.
-- Every function takes the date asked, the AI system and the harmonisation facts and answers through the gate of P2-section-2-gate.l4: NOTHING when Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 do not apply to the system on the date asked,
-- JUST FALSE where Article 2(2) cuts the Article off, NOTHING where Article 2(13) says it may be limited. Reading a result: JUST TRUE the requirement is met; JUST FALSE the text says no; NOTHING not covered.
-- Seam found (not in the plan): paragraph 3 reaches "high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1 (a), of Annex III" (remote biometric identification systems); Annex III is outside my ranges, so the question whether the system is one of them is a plain yes or no.

§ `Article 12(1): automatic recording of events`

-- src:320 | 1. High-risk AI systems shall technically allow for the automatic recording of events (logs) over the lifetime of the system.
@ref Art 12(1) (src:320)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system technically allows for the automatic recording of events (logs) over the lifetime of the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(1) the high-risk AI system technically allows for the automatic recording of events over the lifetime of the system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 12, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the high-risk AI system technically allows for the automatic recording of events (logs) over the lifetime of the system`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "High-risk AI systems shall technically allow for the automatic recording of events (logs) over the lifetime of the system"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 12(2): what the logging capabilities enable`

-- src:321 | 2. In order to ensure a level of traceability of the functioning of a high-risk AI system that is appropriate to the intended purpose of the system, logging capabilities shall enable the recording of events relevant for:
-- src:322 | (a) identifying situations that may result in the high-risk AI system presenting a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1) or in a substantial modification;
-- src:323 | (b) facilitating the post-market monitoring referred to in Article 72; and
-- src:324 | (c) monitoring the operation of high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 26(5).
@ref Art 12(2) (src:321-324)
-- The chapeau ("In order to ensure a level of traceability of the functioning of a high-risk AI system that is appropriate to the intended purpose") gives the purpose; the three listed matters are joined by "and" (the last two) and all are needed.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the logging capabilities enable the recording of events relevant for identifying situations that may result in the high-risk AI system presenting a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1) or in a substantial modification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the logging capabilities enable the recording of events relevant for facilitating the post-market monitoring referred to in Article 72` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the logging capabilities enable the recording of events relevant for monitoring the operation of high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 26(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(2) the logging capabilities enable the recording of events relevant for the purposes listed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 12, "", 2)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the logging capabilities enable the recording of events relevant for identifying situations that may result in the high-risk AI system presenting a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1) or in a substantial modification` AND `the logging capabilities enable the recording of events relevant for facilitating the post-market monitoring referred to in Article 72` AND `the logging capabilities enable the recording of events relevant for monitoring the operation of high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 26(5)`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In order to ensure a level of traceability ... logging capabilities shall enable the recording of events relevant for:"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 12(3): the minimum logs of a remote biometric identification system`

-- src:325 | 3. For high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1 (a), of Annex III, the logging capabilities shall provide, at a minimum:
-- src:326 | (a) recording of the period of each use of the system (start date and time and end date and time of each use);
-- src:327 | (b) the reference database against which input data has been checked by the system;
-- src:328 | (c) the input data for which the search has led to a match;
-- src:329 | (d) the identification of the natural persons involved in the verification of the results, as referred to in Article 14(5).
@ref Art 12(3) (src:325-329)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1 (a), of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the logging capabilities provide a recording of the period of each use of the system (start date and time and end date and time of each use)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the logging capabilities provide a record of the reference database against which input data has been checked by the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the logging capabilities provide a record of the input data for which the search has led to a match` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the logging capabilities provide the identification of the natural persons involved in the verification of the results, as referred to in Article 14(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 12(3) the logging capabilities provide, at a minimum, the recording listed for systems referred to in point 1 (a) of Annex III` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 12, "", 3)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1 (a), of Annex III`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1 (a), of Annex III": the paragraph reaches those systems and no others (seam: Annex III point 1(a))
        ELSE JUST (`the logging capabilities provide a recording of the period of each use of the system (start date and time and end date and time of each use)` AND `the logging capabilities provide a record of the reference database against which input data has been checked by the system` AND `the logging capabilities provide a record of the input data for which the search has led to a match` AND `the logging capabilities provide the identification of the natural persons involved in the verification of the results, as referred to in Article 14(5)`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the logging capabilities shall provide, at a minimum:"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed
